        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "24df1c0a-c673-58ed-998e-022f2a8c58d9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Denmark Hill, Camberwell, London Borough of Southwark, London, Wanganui, New Zealand\n- Landmarks: Big Ben, Palace of Westminster\n- People: Frank William Gilligan\n- Organizations: Oxford University, Essex county side\n- Topics: cricket\n\nFacts:\n- Denmark Hill is an area and road in Camberwell, in the London Borough of Southwark.\n- On a clear day, one can read the time on the Big Ben clockface from Denmark Hill.\n- Frank William Gilligan was born on 20 September 1893 in Denmark Hill, London.\n- Big Ben is the nickname for the Great Bell of the clock at the north end of the Palace of Westminster in London.\n- Big Ben usually also refers to both the clock and the clock tower.\n- Frank William Gilligan was an English cricketer who played for Oxford University and was an integral part of the Essex county side for ten years.\n- Frank William Gilligan died on 4 May 1960 in Wanganui, New Zealand.",
